[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861171737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2861171737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2861171737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qigQZ","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T01:44:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T08:50:51Z","body":"Nice!\r\n\r\n| Master | PR |\r\n|--------|--------|\r\n| ![before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/24b1c9e0-7012-4bf5-bc6d-69e1f916ca24) | ![after](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4329009a-f744-4624-8b7c-284a796528d1) |\r\n| ![before2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d83f5c75-f426-465a-9cd7-ef3f19763cc6) | ![after2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b0431ab2-6a8d-41a4-87a7-15be562a8156) |\r\n\r\n_Edit: In my initial test above I was using tonemapper exposure to make the resulting image brighter. However per @lander-vr's suggestion I tried to use camera exposure instead. This brought out reflections on open surfaces more, while corners still remain occluded, which gives a better result:_\r\n\r\n![after4](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed138c90-5f1e-4d3a-b80a-61021fe2f76c)\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861171737/reactions","total_count":34,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":34,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2864827089","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2864827089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2864827089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qwcrR","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T01:16:31Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T01:16:31Z","body":"This might sound silly, but I've noticed a strange behavior while testing this PR. When you have a metallic material and you gradually reduce its roughness value, it undergoes a transition where the material abruptly changes from a dark color to a lighter one. This doesn't happen when you disable specular occlusion.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/499c505c-d161-4a27-ac10-cda27d2c5404\r\n\r\nIs this expected behavior?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2864827089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865827113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2865827113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2865827113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q0Q0p","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T09:25:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T11:54:08Z","body":"@LiveTrower Mmmh, I cannot seem to reproduce this/notice any strange behavior.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/afe60da3-5c45-4baa-a673-04780496239e\r\n\r\nWhat's happening in your video seems to be expected, I don't think this behavior is unusual. The effect is darkening specular lighting where ambient lighting is darker (In this case on faces with normals facing downwards),\r\n`float reflective_f = (1.0 - roughness) * metallic;` ensures that metallic materials preserve more of their reflection strength, so the effect of specular occlusion is reduced as you decrease the roughness.\r\n\r\nI don't think what's shown in your video looks out of the ordinary. Specular occlusion adds a little more depth to reflective surfaces, so it's normal for it to not be an exact match to when it is disabled.\r\n\r\n@clayjohn What do you think?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865827113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2866231987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2866231987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2866231987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q1zqz","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T11:42:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T14:35:41Z","body":"After testing a little more, while I still cannot reproduce the exact effect of whats happening in your video, it looks like a culprit may be that fully rough surfaces still receive specular lighting. This seems to be the case both for metallic and non-metallic materials.\r\nAs far as I'm aware, a fully rough PBR material, regardless of metalness, should have no specular lighting. It seems like this is not the case for Godots shader. I'm not sure if that is expected due to assumptions being made in the BRDF, or if this is unintentional.\r\n\r\nThere should be no difference between these two as they're both fully rough:\r\n| Metal 0.0 - Specular 0.0 - Rough 1.0 | Metal 0.0 - Specular 1.0 - Rough 1.0 |\r\n| - | - |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6247e90d-7b00-4c3c-9b24-5f9a66ad7b60) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/25036cfb-dad5-4bee-ae3f-5dccd8886420) |\r\n\r\nIt's not a perfect comparison, but if we compare a fully rough principled shader to a diffuse shader in Blender, we see an exact match:\r\n| Blender Diffuse BSDF | Blender Principled BSDF |\r\n| - | - |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/968aae13-c825-4b09-8875-e91e2a23ba16) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1d297b1-9916-4687-8c20-f3eb529527bf) |\r\n\r\nThis is also the reason why when LiveTrower toggles the `disable specular occlusion` flag in their video we see a change in shading on their 100% rough material.\r\n\r\nEither way, this is not something caused by how specular occlusion is tackled by this PR though. After having tested again with a bunch of different ambient light strengths I think it's safe to say that the feature does behave as expected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2866231987/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867076188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2867076188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2867076188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q5Bxc","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T15:54:16Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T15:54:16Z","body":"@lander-vr As far as I know, default Godot shaders use diffuse Lambert by default, and StandardMaterials use diffuse Burley by default, so that could explain a different behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867076188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867102930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#issuecomment-2867102930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106145","id":2867102930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q5ITS","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T16:05:05Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T16:05:31Z","body":"> It's not a perfect comparison, but if we compare a fully rough principled shader to a diffuse shader in Blender, we see an exact match:\r\n\r\nIt's not an exact match. I will provide a very exaggerated example.\r\nBoth materials are on default settings other than roughness being 1.0 on Principled BSDF and color being solid black.\r\nColor Management exposure is also set to 5.0.\r\n| Diffuse BSDF | Principled BSDF |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachm